# {{ADAPTER_NAME}} PSBT adapter

This project is a generated TypeScript parser adapter for [PSBT Interop Lab](https://github.com/GautamBytes/psbt-interop-lab). It uses `bitcoinjs-lib` for native PSBT parsing and implements the lab's bounded JSONL adapter protocol.

## Verify locally

```bash
npm ci
npm test
npm run conformance
```

The lockfile pins every dependency to an exact version. Its `psbt-interop-lab` entry pins version
`{{LAB_VERSION}}` and the matching HTTPS registry tarball but intentionally has no `integrity`
field: this template is contained by that same tarball, so it cannot contain its own digest. Other
dependencies retain their published integrity values. After version `{{LAB_VERSION}}` is available
from npm, projects whose policy requires an SRI value can hydrate that one entry before committing
the generated lockfile:

```bash
npm install --save-dev --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts psbt-interop-lab@{{LAB_VERSION}}
```

The adapter currently declares parser-only support for PSBTv0. Extend its capabilities only when the corresponding operations are implemented and tested.

## Identity before publishing results

The generated adapter reports `generated-typescript-template-v1` as its source revision so the scaffold works immediately. Before treating a compatibility report as release evidence, replace that value in both `src/adapter.ts` and `adapter-manifest.json` with the exact wallet or library revision under test.

The adapter hashes its compiled entrypoint and self-reports that value as `artifactDigest`, as required by the protocol. This detects a changed entrypoint but is not runtime attestation and does not cover the dependency tree. Pin `expected.artifactDigest` in the manifest only when your build can independently reproduce and verify the artifact that runs.
